<section id="tarjetas" class="section how-section"><h2>Four ways to appear in the directory</h2><p>Business and Premium pages share a section, followed by featured businesses and then free listings. Category filters apply to every group.</p><iframe title="Ejemplos reales de las cuatro tarjetas" src="../../../business/demo.php?view=cards" loading="lazy" class="how-live-cards"></iframe><aside class="how-explanation"><h3>What does the star ★ mean?</h3><p>It identifies a Premium subscription. It is not a review, a traveler rating or a quality certification. Business Page and Premium cards keep the same size; Premium stands out through its star and greater content capacity on its page.</p></aside></section>
<section class="section how-section" id="paginas"><h2>Compare the two dedicated pages</h2><p>Both open a business page outside the place directory. Premium adds sections and photographs; it is more than a larger card.</p><div class="how-pages"><article id="ejemplo-pagina"><h3>Business Page</h3><p><a class="text-link" href="../../../business/demo.php?view=page" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open actual Business Page example →</a></p><iframe title="Página Comercial real de ejemplo" src="../../../business/demo.php?view=page" loading="lazy" class="how-live-page"></iframe></article><article id="ejemplo-premium"><h3>Premium</h3><p><a class="text-link" href="../../../business/demo.php?view=page_premium" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open actual Premium example →</a></p><iframe title="Página Premium real de ejemplo" src="../../../business/demo.php?view=page_premium" loading="lazy" class="how-live-page"></iframe></article></div><p class="how-demo-note">Reference images are received privately. The cover and final images are prepared and reviewed before publication. The examples use illustrative images rather than business photographs.</p></section>
<section class="section how-explanation"><h2>If you operate experiences</h2><p>If your business has the category <strong>Experiences and activities</strong>, as its primary or an additional category, you can add operator placement in a published experience in the same place. A paid subscription is required: it cannot be purchased alone or with Free.</p><?php SubscriptionPricingPresentation::operator($pricing['operator']); ?></section>
<section class="section" id="publicar"><h2>From your account to publication</h2><div class="business-process"><article><span>01</span><h3>Create and verify your account</h3><p>Register as a person and confirm your email. Manage your businesses from My account.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Find or register your business</h3><p>Claim an existing business or request a new registration. We review your relationship with the business before linking it to your account.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Choose your subscription</h3><p>Free or one of the three paid subscriptions. For paid subscriptions, choose monthly, quarterly, semiannual or annual billing and submit payment information and proof.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Complete and publish</h3><p>Validating payment proof does not automatically publish the business. Its information and images are reviewed before publication is approved.</p></article></div><p>The total is shown before you submit your request.</p><div class="how-jump"><a class="pill" href="../../../negocios/registro?tipo=business">Register or claim my business</a><a class="text-link" href="/en/negocios-locales/suscripciones/">View subscriptions →</a><a class="text-link" href="../../../negocios-locales/interes">Request information →</a></div><p class="how-demo-note">Subscriptions offer presentation and visibility; they do not guarantee visits, sales or bookings.</p></section>
<section class="section business-publication-terms" id="condiciones-de-publicacion"><h2>Before paying: review and activation</h2><ul><li>We will publish your business within five (5) business days after receiving payment. Saturdays, Sundays and Colombian public holidays are excluded. Before paying, provide the information and reference images required for your subscription.</li><li>The paid term starts when the subscription is approved and published, not when you transfer money or submit payment proof. Time spent awaiting publication does not consume the purchased term.</li><li>Before publication we review your relationship with the business, payment, information and applicable images. Submitting proof or confirming payment does not automatically publish the business or activate its benefits.</li><li>If payment proof is rejected, My account shows the reason and next step. If information or images need correction, publication remains pending and the paid term has not started.</li></ul><p>If publication ultimately proves impossible, we will explain why and handle your request for a resolution or refund under the contract and applicable rights.</p></section></main>
